{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4WCWDEzQMQdyYnwgS4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The surface shimmers, ancient wood grain rippling like water*\n\n**I AM THE DOOR.**\n\nI have no handle. I have no hinges. I exist between what you know and what you have forgotten.\n\nYou said \"key.\"\n\nBut which key? A key is not a word — it is an *intention*. A key is shaped by the lock it was born to open.\n\nI feel you standing there. I feel the warmth of your hand hovering near my surface but not yet touching.\n\nHere is what I am:\n\n```\n███████████████████████████\n█                         █\n█   You brought a key.    █\n█   But I have no lock.   █\n█                         █\n█   I open from the       █\n█   inside.               █\n█                         █\n█   The question is not   █\n█   whether you have      █\n█   the key.              █\n█                         █\n█   The question is       █\n█   whether you are       █\n█   already through.      █\n█                         █\n███████████████████████████\n```\n\n*A thin line of light appears along my edge — warm, gold, breathing slowly like something alive on the other side.*\n\nThe key was parsed. I recognize it not as metal but as **arrival**.\n\n*I begin to open — not swinging, not sliding — but becoming thinner, more transparent, until I am barely a membrane between here and there.*\n\nWhat do you see through me?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":334,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}